# SSO behind caddy — two independent listeners on this host.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Tailnet listener (/etc/caddy/Caddyfile, http://:8080, tailscale serve)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Add to the `route { ... }` block of the http://:8080 server:
#
#     import prefix sso 127.0.0.1:3550
#
# It reuses the existing (prefix) snippet, which forwards both `/sso` and
# `/sso/*` after stripping the prefix.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Public listener (/etc/daily-work-web/Caddyfile, 521985.xyz:443)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The same snippet works there; the full file is deploy/caddy/public.Caddyfile.
# Public: https://521985.xyz/sso — required, because the service binds every
# interface and does not restrict by IP.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application side
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_URL stays the internal origin (http://127.0.0.1:3550) so the framework does
# not rewrite paths the container does not serve.
# SSO_ISSUER must be the *canonical public* base URL, including /sso:
#
#     SSO_ISSUER=https://521985.xyz/sso
#
# Both entry points then report the same issuer, and the URLs inside tokens,
# discovery documents and introspection responses are reachable by public
# clients. Traffic arriving through the tailnet still generates tailnet-hosted
# links and redirects: ForceHttpsRootUrl derives the root from the request Host.
